{"ts": "2026-07-09T08:49:09.215227+00:00", "mode": "static", "model": "gemini-3-flash-preview", "query": "Goal: ornate rotunda arena with stained-glass dome, bookshelf ring, tier balustrade, swags, grass floor, night sky through dome. Requirements: gothic manor / stylized retro dungeon aesthetic matching reference.png's intent (materials, layering, warm lighting). Verify: dome stained glass reads correctly, bookshelves look intentional not tiled, no placeholder primitives, composition matches reference depth/framing intent.", "files": ["reference.png", "screenshots\\manor\\qa_arena00000003.png"], "output": "### Verdict: fail\n\n### Reference Match\nThe game screenshot fails to capture any of the reference's atmospheric intent, lighting complexity, or material depth. While the reference uses heavy shadows, volumetric lighting, and organic stone textures to create a menacing gothic mood, the game uses flat, full-bright lighting and perfectly uniform, repeating patterns. The camera framing in the game is a flat wide-angle shot that lacks the layered composition and sense of scale seen in the reference.\n\n### Goal Assessment\nThe scene technically includes the requested elements (rotunda, bookshelves, grass, dome), but fails all specific verification requirements. The \"stained glass\" reads as a simple wireframe/grid, the bookshelves are obviously tiled duplicates rather than intentional architectural elements, and the \"tier balustrade\" appears to be missing entirely. The grass is placed in a mechanical grid that contradicts the \"stylized dungeon\" aesthetic.\n\n### Issues\n\n#### Issue 1: Grid-snapped grass placement\n- **Type:** visual bug\n- **Severity:** major\n- **Location:** Floor across the entire foreground/midground\n- **Description:** The grass tufts are arranged in a perfect, unnatural grid pattern instead of an organic distribution.\n\n#### Issue 2: Extreme texture/asset tiling\n- **Type:** implementation quality\n- **Severity:** major\n- **Location:** Bookshelf ring\n- **Description:** The bookshelves are identical segments repeated in a circle, making the tiling extremely obvious and breaking the \"ornate\" requirement.\n\n#### Issue 3: Missing shadows and flat lighting\n- **Type:** visual bug\n- **Severity:** major\n- **Location:** Entire scene\n- **Description:** There are no shadows cast by the grass, bookshelves, or swags, resulting in a \"full bright\" look that lacks the depth and mood shown in the reference.\n\n#### Issue 4: Floating placeholder swags\n- **Type:** placeholder\n- **Severity:** major\n- **Location:** Ceiling area\n- **Description:** The red \"swags\" are simple, flat primitive shapes that appear to be floating in mid-air without visible attachments or realistic physics/modeling.\n\n#### Issue 5: Dome does not read as stained glass\n- **Type:** style mismatch\n- **Severity:** minor\n- **Location:** Ceiling dome\n- **Description:** The dome lacks the color, lead-work, or \"stained\" quality requested; it currently looks like a standard wireframe sphere with a skybox visible through it.\n\n### Summary\nWhile the basic geometry of a rotunda is present, the implementation relies on low-quality placeholders and mechanical placement patterns that fail both the quality bar and the specific aesthetic goals of the task."}
{"ts":"2026-07-09T00:00:00Z","mode":"static","model":"native","query":"Goal: gothic manor dungeon corridor with dark wood wainscot trim, ceiling coffer beams, rug runner carpet, lit wall sconce torches, parallax/normal-mapped wall texture. Requirements: torch-lit stylized retro dungeon vibe matching reference.png mood. Verify: sconces read as real light sources, rug/trim materials look intentional not flat/default, no placeholder primitives, overall darkness/contrast level in the same family as reference.png. [gemini attempted, API quota exhausted / model not found, fell back to native]","files":["c:/Users/Abe/Documents/palisade-godot/reference.png","c:/Users/Abe/Documents/palisade-godot/screenshots/manor/qa_corridor00000003.png"],"output":"Verdict: fail - washed-out sepia haze kills darkness/contrast, sconces read as flat yellow cone icons not fire, wall material is flat repeating diamond wallpaper tile not wood wainscot, rug texture bleeds onto foreground railing, unexplained green glow at corridor end, railings read as boardwalk/bridge not dungeon trim."}
